{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "39987959-f0b6-878f-b638-1aa534a54f5b",
  "created_at": "2026-01-30T15:48:49-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, City Clerk",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Rosa Rivera",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sandra Pimentel",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:46:30-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "City Clerk's office, this is Sandra. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:46:34-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yes, thith is Rosa. Sorry, I just got out of the car and I'm juth walking in from the parking lot. Um, so I was up early today, my mother had a doctor thing, and then I figured I'd finally make the calls I've been putting off."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:46:47-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, I know that kind of Friday. Go ahead, Rosa, what are you calling about?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:46:52-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so my mom needs a passport, and she needs a certified copy of her birth certificate. She was born in Newport. I think. Well, she was born at the hospital here, so that's Newport, right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:47:02-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "If she was born in Newport, we'd have the record here. Is she the one who'll be requesting it, or are you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:47:09-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Me, I guess? I'm calling for her. Is that okay? I'm her daughter. Sorry, my mouth is being weird, I think it's the cold. Thith is, this is better now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:47:18-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, I can hear you fine. A child can usually request a parent's record, you'd just need to show who you are. Do you have your own photo ID?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:47:26-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I have my license. But the passport people said it has to be the long one, the one with the seal? Is that the certified one, or is that different from the one with the, the hospital footprints?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:47:36-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, the footprints one is a keepsake from the hospital. You want the certified copy from us, with the raised seal. That's the one the passport office accepts."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:47:44-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay. So I'd need the certified one, not the, the abstract thing? Someone told me there's a short version."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:47:50-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good question. Ask for the full certified copy, that's the safe one for a passport. The short versions can get rejected."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:47:56-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, full certified. And how long does it take? She has a trip in the spring, so I don't know if that's tight."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:48:03-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "If you come in with ID, it's often done while you wait or close to it. By mail it takes longer, usually a week or two depending on the mail. Spring should be fine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:48:12-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, good. Wait, so I can just walk in? Do I need her to come too? Or a note from her?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:48:18-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'd bring a signed note from her along with your ID, just to be safe. And her full name and date of birth, plus her parents' names if you have them."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:48:27-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so the note, my ID, her info. And the full one. Sorry, I'm writing this on the back of an envelope. Can you say the note part again?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:48:35-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. A short signed note from your mom saying you can request it for her. Bring your license, and we'll take it from there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:48:42-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. I think I have it. Thank you so much, Sandra."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T15:48:46-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Rosa. Have a nice weekend."
    }
  ],
